\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Use regex on a string\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 The result of 
\f2\fs26 bash
\f1\fs24 's regex matching can be used to replace 
\f2\fs26 sed
\f1\fs24  for a large number of use-cases.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 CAVEAT
\f1\b0 : This is one of the few platform dependent 
\f2\fs26 bash
\f1\fs24  features. 
\f2\fs26 bash
\f1\fs24  will use whatever regex engine is installed on the user's system. Stick to POSIX regex features if aiming for compatibility.\

\f0\b CAVEAT
\f1\b0 : This example only prints the first matching group. When using multiple capture groups some modification is needed.\

\f0\b Example Function:
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0 regex() \{\
    # Usage: regex "string" "regex"\
    [[ $1 =~ $2 ]] && printf '%s\\n' "$\{BASH_REMATCH[1]\}"\
\}\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs24 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 Example Usage:
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0 $ # Trim leading white-space.\
$ regex '    hello' '^\\s*(.*)'\
hello\
\
$ # Validate a hex color.\
$ regex "#FFFFFF" '^(#?([a-fA-F0-9]\{6\}|[a-fA-F0-9]\{3\}))$'\
#FFFFFF\
\
$ # Validate a hex color (invalid).\
$ regex "red" '^(#?([a-fA-F0-9]\{6\}|[a-fA-F0-9]\{3\}))$'\
# no output (invalid)\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs24 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 Example Usage in script:
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0 is_hex_color() \{\
    if [[ $1 =~ ^(#?([a-fA-F0-9]\{6\}|[a-fA-F0-9]\{3\}))$ ]]; then\
        printf '%s\\n' "$\{BASH_REMATCH[1]\}"\
    else\
        printf '%s\\n' "error: $1 is an invalid color."\
        return 1\
    fi\
\}\
\
read -r color\
is_hex_color "$color" || color="#FFFFFF"\
\
# Do stuff.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

