\f0\b\fs48 \cf0 TRAPS\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Traps allow a script to execute code on various signals. In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://github.com/dylanaraps/pxltrm"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 pxltrm}} (
\f3\i a pixel art editor written in bash
\f1\i0 ) traps are used to redraw the user interface on window resize. Another use case is cleaning up temporary files on script exit.\
Traps should be added near the start of scripts so any early errors are also caught.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 NOTE:
\f1\b0  For a full list of signals, see 
\f2\fs26 trap -l
\f1\fs24 .\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Do something on script exit\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs26 \cf0 # Clear screen on script exit.\
trap 'printf \\\\e[2J\\\\e[H\\\\e[m' EXIT\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs24 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Ignore terminal interrupt (CTRL+C, SIGINT)\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs26 \cf0 trap '' INT\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs24 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 React to window resize\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs26 \cf0 # Call a function on window resize.\
trap 'code_here' SIGWINCH\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs24 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Do something before every command\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs26 \cf0 trap 'code_here' DEBUG\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs24 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Do something when a shell function or a sourced file finishes executing\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs26 \cf0 trap 'code_here' RETURN\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

