\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Run a command in the background\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 This will run the given command and keep it running, even after the terminal or SSH connection is terminated. All output is ignored.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0 bkr() \{\
    (nohup "$@" &>/dev/null &)\
\}\
\
bkr ./some_script.sh # some_script.sh is now running in the background\
